Cell["\<\
group may be a database identifier such as gray[n] or the corresponding \
magnetic-group number.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b677d726-2622-41a4-9f8f-55a023b234a9"],

Cell["\<\
Each row gives a representative position. Symbols x, y, and z are free \
Wyckoff coordinates; the moment entry gives the directions allowed by the \
site symmetry. The multiplicity is the number of equivalent positions in the \
conventional cell.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"78107069-118e-4855-8d37-7def31779a83"]
}, Closed]],

